  "disposition": "firing",
  "family": "value normalization — comment-ONLY value (the case mutation exposed)",
  "defeats": "a `\\s+#` comment anchor, and the absorption that hid its absence. `FIELD_RE` already eats the spaces after the colon, so this value reaches the normalizer as `# unbound, ...` with no leading whitespace: a `\\s+#` anchor never fires, the first-token split then yields the single character `#`, and the field is reported as `that is not a kp:// URN` when the true fact is that it declares NO VALUE and invariant 1 was never checked. This is the ONLY case in the set whose verdict the comment strip alone decides — every other comment-bearing case is covered by the first-token split as well, which is why dropping the strip left the suite green at 23/23 until this case existed."
}
